# Rockpocket iPod - Monolith's lists, an iPod 5.5 for the now playing screen.
#
# Two thirds of the panel is the iPod's screen, the last third the click
# wheel - roughly the proportions of the real thing, where the wheel is a
# good deal smaller than the display above it.
#
# The wheel is a picture and nothing is bound to it. The stick still owns
# the panel, and a wheel that looked live but was not would be worse than
# one that plainly is not. Its job is to say what this screen is.
#
# Two rules this file exists to obey, both learned the hard way:
#
#   * A viewport clears its background. Nothing below may overlap anything
#     above it, or the later one wipes the earlier one off the screen.
#   * Nothing may come after the viewport that draws the wheel. The skin
#     engine redraws every loaded image at the end of every viewport it
#     renders, ignoring which viewport that is, so a later viewport gets
#     the wheel stamped over its contents. That is why the MENU label is
#     baked into the bitmap instead of being skin text.
#
# The wheel bitmap is generated by tools/gen_clickwheel.c - the skin engine
# has no circle primitive, so the shape is baked rather than drawn.

%wd

# Position is viewport-relative, and the wheel's viewport is placed exactly
# where the bitmap goes, so the bitmap sits at its own origin inside it.
%xl(W,clickwheel-480x800x16.bmp,0,0)

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the screen
#
# An iPod's now playing screen: a header strip with the play state, the
# position in the playlist and the battery; album art on the left with the
# track, artist and album stacked beside it; the scrubber along the bottom
# with elapsed on the left and time remaining, negative, on the right.

# The glass itself, one shade off the body.
%V(20,30,440,470,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Vf(F4F2EE)

# header
%V(20,30,440,42,-)
%Vb(262B36)
%Vf(C9CED8)
%al%?if(%mp,=,2)<%|%||%>>%ac%pp of %pe%ar%bl%%

# album art, left, the way the 5.5 stacks it
%Cl(0,0,200,200,c,c)
%?C<%Vd(art)|%Vd(noart)>

%Vl(art,36,96,200,200,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Cd

# No artwork is not an empty square: the real thing puts a plain note
# placeholder there, and a flat panel reads the same way.
%Vl(noart,36,96,200,200,-)
%Vb(1F2531)

# Track, artist, album - stacked to the right of the art, the title picked
# out and the other two dropped back, as the real thing does.
#
# Two viewports rather than one with a colour change partway down: %Vf is a
# viewport setting, not something to switch mid-content.
%V(252,96,192,64,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Vf(F4F2EE)
%s%?it<%it|%fn>

%V(252,164,192,132,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Vf(9AA1AE)
%s%?ia<%ia|%?iA<%iA|%(unknown artist%)>>
%s%?id<%id|%?d(1)<%d(1)|>>

# elapsed and remaining, either end of the scrubber
#
# 34 px, not 28: the theme sets an 18 px font, but a viewport shorter than
# the line height of whatever font is loaded draws nothing at all, and one
# only a little taller drops the descenders onto the scrubber below it.
%V(36,404,408,34,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Vf(9AA1AE)
%al%pc%ar-%pr

# the scrubber
%V(36,444,408,18,-)
%Vb(141821)
%Vf(C9CED8)
%pb(0,4,408,8)

# --------------------------------------------------------------- the wheel
#
# Exactly the size of the bitmap, and last in the file. See the two rules
# at the top - both of them are about this viewport.
%V(104,514,272,272,-)
%xd(W)
